      "content": "When the foundation feels completely gone, the idea of \"building\" can feel impossible, which is a heavy weight to carry. Sometimes, instead of trying to build something grand, the focus can shift to simply *caring* for the small, immediate needs of yourself. Even tiny acts of self-compassion, like rest or a short walk, are valid steps forward. Please consider connecting with a crisis line if the feeling of hopelessness becomes overwhelming, as they are trained to help in these exact moments.",
